{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789241134,"nonce":"QpOvYMLBVl8H7Amp9NIW5KFUW7I=","title":"Python: function values are complete for defs and lambdas; three gaps remain","message":"Function values are records `[code, arity, cells...]` boxed under\nFUNC_TAG, called through `zb_call_N`, with closure conversion through\none-element list cells and `nonlocal` writes to them. Gaps:\n\n1. A default on a lambda or nested def parameter is rejected: a call\n   through a value passes exactly N arguments, so the record would need\n   a minimum arity and the code a \"missing\" marker per parameter.\n2. A builtin as a value (`map(str, xs)`, `apply(len, x)`) is not a\n   record. `int`, `str` and the other type names are strings so that\n   `type(x) == int` holds; making them records means `type()` must\n   return the same record and records must compare by code address.\n3. Calls through values take at most 8 arguments (MAX_CALL_ARITY).","files":null}]}